+# Coupled run status
+
+Run the native command or the installed npm entry point:
+
+```text
+spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+spiral coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`PATH` is resolved relative to the caller's current working directory. The
+command is read-only: it inspects `iterations.json` and native
+`state/tui-work.json` ledgers without provider calls, tool execution, API keys,
+or workspace changes.
+
+`wire_requests` counts every durable request in `requests`. `task_requests`
+counts requests charged to the task budget; omitted native `charge` defaults to
+task. Failed and in-flight attempts are counted, while logs and prose are
+never used as evidence.
+
+Interrupted runs can have unknown pending usage. A missing pending ledger is
+reported as `null`, never zero; limits remain known, but used and remaining
+aggregate usage is unknown. Existing malformed pending data is an error.
+
+`completed` is the native recorded lifecycle result. It is not independent
+verification, qualification, or promotion authorization.
+
+The completed synthetic example from `scripts.status_fixture.make`, exactly
+matching `scripts.status_fixture.expected('completed')`, is:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"status":"completed","stop_reason":"completed","iterations":[{"iteration":1,"task_id":"t1","termination":"completed","task_requests":2,"wire_requests":3,"changed_files":["src/a.rs"],"newly_verified":["cargo test -q"]}],"pending":null,"requests":{"task_used":2,"wire_used":3,"task_limit":192,"wire_limit":216,"task_remaining":190,"wire_remaining":213}}
+```
